{
  "title": "Plane \u2014 productivity, project-management, issue-tracking (49,511\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Plane\nDomain: productivity, project-management, issue-tracking | Scale: large | Stars: 49,511\nProblem: Plane is an open-source project management platform that provides a modern alternative to Jira, Linear, Monday, and ClickUp for managing tasks, sprints, documents, and product roadmaps without the overhead of complex tool management.\nTarget users: Engineering teams, Product managers, Project managers, Organizations seeking self-hosted project management, Teams requiring issue tracking and sprint planning\nCore features: Work Items - Create and manage tasks with rich text editor, file uploads, and issue references; Cycles - Sprint-like functionality with burn-down charts and progress tracking; Modules - Divide complex projects into manageable components; Customizable Views - Create filtered views and save/share them with teams; Pages - Capture ideas with AI capabilities and rich text editor; Analytics - Real-time insights and trend visualization across project data; Kanban/Gantt Board Support - Multiple visualization options for workflows\nIntegrations: Cloud deployment (Plane Cloud), Docker containerization, Kubernetes orchestration, Instance admin God mode for self-hosted configuration\nTech stack: React, React Router, TypeScript, Vite, Next.js + Django, Node.js, Python + PostgreSQL + Docker, Kubernetes, Redis\nKey libraries: React Router, Django, ProseMirror (rich text editing), Turbo (monorepo management), Valibot (validation), Markdown-it, Husky (git hooks), Oxlint/Oxfmt (code quality)\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Monorepo structure using Turbo for managing multiple packages and coordinated builds across frontend and backend\n- Self-hosted first approach with Docker and Kubernetes support reflects enterprise focus on data privacy and control\n- Feature-rich rich text editing and AI integration indicates emphasis on knowledge capture alongside task management\n- Comprehensive analytics and multiple visualization modes (Kanban, Gantt, custom views) suggest design prioritizes workflow flexibility and team autonomy",
